  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the product of maximum outcome and its probability (which is equivalent to the contribution of the top outcome to expected value in this case). The individual computes expected values, finds them equal, and then resorts to preferring the higher possible gain. While the individual considers the same quantities (outcomes and probabilities), their decision rule is not identical to the given reason. The reason would be indifferent, but the individual breaks indifference by favoring the higher outcome. The verbal report shows awareness of the relevant information (products/outcomes × probabilities), but the justification relies on a secondary heuristic (aiming for the higher gain when expected values are equal and probabilities are low), rather than strictly following the rule of selecting based on the higher product. Thus, the reason is partially aligned but not fully used as a decisive rule.",
